  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract activity in Iowa through FY2026 to date shows a marked pullback in spending compared with recent years. Total federal contract obligations in Iowa are $1.2B, based on partial fiscal-year totals. AwardCount stands at 17,777 and the averageAwardSize is $69.8K. Obligations are down 65.5% year over year. Historically, obligations peaked at $3.6B in FY25 and were $3.4B in FY23; prior years were $3B in FY24, $2.7B in FY22, and $2.5B in FY21. The Department of Defense accounts for the largest share of current-year buying with $789M in obligations, followed by the Department of the Treasury with $158M and the Department of Agriculture with $103M. At the vendor level, ROCKWELL COLLINS, INC. and DATA LINK SOLUTIONS LLC lead with $290M and $253M respectively, and PMX INDUSTRIES, INC. has $103M. Key industry categories include Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $261M, Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying at $103M, and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $101M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did overall obligations fall so sharply in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Obligations are down 65.5% year over year, reflecting a large decline from the $3.6B recorded in FY25 to $1.2B in FY26 to date. That drop appears alongside a smaller buyer base this year: the Department of Defense remains the largest buyer at $789M, but other agencies show much lower totals. The combination of a reduced total spend and a high number of awards keeps the average award at $69.8K. Expect contracting patterns to look different this fiscal year compared with the prior four-year run of higher obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate current-year contracting in Iowa?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer with $789M, followed by the Department of the Treasury at $158M and the Department of Agriculture at $103M. On the vendor side, ROCKWELL COLLINS, INC. is the largest recipient with $290M, followed by DATA LINK SOLUTIONS LLC at $253M and PMX INDUSTRIES, INC. at $103M. Industry concentration is highest in Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing with $261M and related manufacturing and engineering categories totaling multiple high-value lines."
      }
    ]
  },
